Generate a cohesive family of full-bleed Urkaaaz Loadout ammunition-card
illustrations.

Create five separate images, with one image-generation request per ammunition
type. Do not combine the outputs into a grid, montage, contact sheet, collage,
or sprite sheet.

## Reference inputs

- Attach the Urkaaaz main-menu background as the primary palette and
  atmosphere reference. Use its blue sky, warm clouds, golden light, green
  landscape, and earthy materials without copying the complete composition
  into every card.
- Attach the current icon for each ammunition type. Each icon is the
  authoritative identity reference for that card's projectile or ammunition
  object. Preserve its recognizable design, silhouette, colors, and defining
  details; do not redesign the item.
- Attach one approved Urkaaaz unit-card illustration as a secondary style and
  scale reference so the ammunition cards belong to the same Loadout art
  family.
- The current icon can use a different pose or camera angle, but do not invent
  ammunition types, gameplay effects, abilities, faction marks, or defining
  equipment absent from its reference.

## Art direction

- Each image is a portrait, full-bleed illustration intended to fill one
  complete Loadout carousel card. Make the referenced ammunition item large,
  central, and immediately recognizable at mobile-card size.
- Match the approved unit-card finish: painterly fantasy-game rendering,
  dimensional hand-painted forms, warm cinematic light, controlled
  saturation, clear silhouettes, and detailed but uncluttered materials.
- Keep all five cards visually cohesive in camera distance, subject scale,
  lighting direction, contrast, detail density, and background palette.
- Use a soft-focus battlefield or campaign setting inspired by the supplied
  main-menu background. Keep scenery subdued behind the ammunition item.
- Compose for a narrow portrait card. Keep the main object and its defining
  silhouette inside the central 80% of the image; do not crop important
  features at the edges.
- Reserve the lower 22% for a darker, low-detail area behind Android's
  slightly translucent title strip. The item name and any stock or cost
  metadata are live UI text; do not bake text into the illustration.
- Keep the upper-left and upper-right corners visually simple for Android's
  separate information and selected-check icons.
- The illustration fills the whole card but must contain no card frame,
  border, selected outline, check badge, information button, lock icon, text,
  or control. Android renders those layers separately.
- Do not reproduce the supplied icon as a small inset badge. Integrate the
  referenced ammunition object into the full-card composition while
  preserving its identity.

## Output format

- Produce exactly one independent PNG per ammunition type, at exactly
  512 x 720 pixels.
- Use full-bleed opaque backgrounds, portrait composition, and clean edges.
- Never include transparent checkerboards, empty margins, a tiled background,
  or a neighboring card in the output.
- Save generated files for review under:
  `assets_src/loadout/ammunition-cards/`
- Do not copy generated images into Android resources until the user approves
  the reviewed previews.
- These are presentation illustrations only. Do not change ammunition
  balance, projectile behavior, simulation visuals, or gameplay assets.

## Output files

1. `loadout_ammunition_rock_card.png` — `ROCK`; use the supplied ROCK icon as
   the exact identity reference.
2. `loadout_ammunition_siege_bomb_card.png` — `SIEGE_BOMB`; use the supplied
   Siege Bomb icon as the exact identity reference.
3. `loadout_ammunition_powder_barrel_card.png` — `POWDER_BARREL`; use the
   supplied Powder Barrel icon as the exact identity reference.
4. `loadout_ammunition_fire_rain_card.png` — `FIRE_RAIN`; use the supplied
   Fire Rain icon as the exact identity reference.
5. `loadout_ammunition_plague_cauldron_card.png` — `PLAGUE_CAULDRON`; use the
   supplied Plague Cauldron icon as the exact identity reference.

## Review checklist

- Verify that all five files are valid 512 x 720 PNGs with opaque,
  full-bleed backgrounds.
- Check that every ammunition type is recognizable at carousel-card size and
  remains consistent with its supplied icon.
- Check that the set matches the supplied background and approved unit-card
  art without copying either reference composition.
- Confirm that the lower title-strip area and both top icon areas remain
  unobstructed.
- Ensure that no image contains text, card trim, icons, controls, watermark,
  or unintended game content.

Show all five assets individually for review. Do not integrate them into
Android resources until approved.
